    {
      "t": "2026-11-13T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "On November 13, 2026, the FAA issued a nationwide ground stop after a Chicago-area communications failure was found to affect multiple systems across the National Airspace System.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1386016697:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-13T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "The agency cited \"extraordinary circumstances involving communications failures\", and the ground stop was later lifted.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-13:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-13T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "A Microsoft global outage had occurred on November 12, 2026, and continued into the morning of the same day as the FAA outage.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1386016697:47"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-13T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "The issues involved communication problems at area control centers in the United States.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1386016697:summary"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-13T00:00:34Z",
      "text": "Bloomberg and Reuters reported the story.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-13:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-13T00:00:42Z",
      "text": "Al Jazeera headlined the story \"US flights resume after FAA lifts hours-long nationwide ground stop\".",
      "cites": [
        "news:aljazeera:706b1608b1a0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-13T00:00:48Z",
      "text": "DW headlined it \"FAA issues US national ground stop on all flights\".",
      "cites": [
        "news:dw:c0cfbcc007e2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-13T00:00:54Z",
      "text": "France 24 headlined it \"US flight authority orders national ground stop over air traffic control 'communication issue'\".",
      "cites": [
        "news:france24:bea6c8926b2d"
      ]
    },
    {
